  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Around the manganese atom, there are five <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CO</mi></math> ligands and one Mn occupying octahedron vertices. For octahedral geometry, the more appropriate hybridization is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> that produces six hybrid orbitals pointing towards <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CO</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mn</mi></math>.</p><p>The octahedral shape of molecules is the shape of molecules where six atoms or ligands or groups of atoms are arranged in a systematic way around a central dogma or atom. The Octahedral Shape of Molecules molecules has eight faces.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0069_a7ca4442c8b6.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 282px;\"/></p></blockquote>"
  }
